From: MakOS Project <makos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] installer: stage MakOS process and JavaScript executables

MakOS uses the Unix flat application directory, not a macOS application
bundle. Include both required executables in Mozilla's package manifest so
stage-package carries the same plugin-container and xpcshell bytes that the
release build stamp authorizes. Other platforms retain their package lists.

XP_MAKOS is provided by the target configure check and reaches the package
preprocessor through the installer's existing ACDEFINES argument.

diff --git a/browser/installer/package-manifest.in b/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
--- a/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
+++ b/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
@@ -86,6 +86,10 @@
 @BINPATH@/@MOZ_CHILD_PROCESS_NAME@.app/
 @BINPATH@/@MOZ_EME_PROCESS_NAME@.app/
 #endif
+#ifdef XP_MAKOS
+@BINPATH@/@MOZ_CHILD_PROCESS_NAME@
+@BINPATH@/xpcshell
+#endif
 #ifdef XP_WIN
 @BINPATH@/@MOZ_CHILD_PROCESS_NAME@
 #if MOZ_PACKAGE_MSVC_DLLS
